Core provider modules

When we convert these requirements into the actual application, I would recommend roughly these 20 major navigation modules instead of exposing all 54 processes as separate menu items:

#	Provider module	Purpose
1	Dashboard	Provider command center
2	Requests	Incoming customer jobs
3	Quotes	Quotations and offers
4	Bookings	Confirmed and active jobs
5	Calendar	Job scheduling
6	Messages	Customer communication
7	Services	Services offered
8	Pricing	Rates and pricing rules
9	Service Areas	Provider coverage
10	Availability	Working schedule
11	Customers	Customer relationships
12	Wallet	Provider money
13	Earnings	Revenue reporting
14	Payouts	Withdrawal management
15	Reviews	Ratings and feedback
16	Performance	Provider KPIs
17	Team	Employees and technicians
18	Documents	Verification/compliance
19	Support	Cases and disputes
20	Settings	Account configuration

The important architectural point is that the Provider App should not merely be a second version of the Customer App. The Customer side is primarily a service-purchasing application, while the Provider side is effectively a small field-service business management system connected to the FIXO marketplace.

That distinction will make the provider platform considerably more powerful and scalable.